WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:08.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.267
-Well, hi, y'all,

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:13.100
and welcome to Todd Taft's
Odd Crafts Podcast.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.100
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.968
I'm Todd Taft.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:17.434
Now, on this show, we take a
look at

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:20.801
the weird and wonderful world
of D-I-Y knickknacks

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.734
that you can T-R-Y at home.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:28.334
Today, we're joined by one of my
favorite crafters,

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.767
but it's his first time on the
show and he's a little nervous.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.868
So please join me
in giving a warm welcome

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.534
to Carole St. James.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.167
Hi, Carole.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.534
-Hi.
-Hi, Todd.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.367
-Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.133
-Oh, I'm sorry, Todd.
I'd shake your hand,

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.234
but my hands are just
covered in Mod Podge.

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.467
-Oh, I've been there, Carole.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.067
What do you have for us today?

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:55.033
-Well, my first one -- and this
is really special to me, Todd.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.868
-Huh.
-This is a little pet sheep.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.167
-Well, look at that.
-And all you need to make these

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:04.634
are toothpicks, a cotton ball,
and the secret ingredient.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.000
-Secret ingredient, what's that,
imagination?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.467
[ Light Laughter ]

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.000
-Those little googly eyes.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.100
-Ah. That's precious.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.634
Does it have a --
does it have a name?

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.067
-Well, that's the great thing
about these, Todd.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.000
You can name them whatever you
want, because they're yours.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.767
But this one is named Diablo.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:26.067
Because he is trouble.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.467
-He -- he looks like a rascal

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:29.868
that just wants to
stay up all night.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.400
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.634
He -- he looks like he wouldn't
wear his seatbelt in the car.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.701
-No, no. Not Diablo.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.834
-No, you won't be
counting him before bed.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.567
-No. Well, let me put this
little guy away

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:40.968
before my heart just melts.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.934
-Oh, wow.
I love this sheep.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:48.601
-So, Carole, how -- how did you
come up with your next item?

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:52.734
-Well, my next item,
when I was young --

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.400
this is a great story, Todd.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.501
-When I was young,
my dad sat me down

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.601
and he gave me
a can and some yarn.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.100
And he said,
"Boy, go make something."

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.767
-Wow.
-So I came up with this.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:05.767
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:08.467
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:10.968
Now -- now, what do --
what do you call that?

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.100
-Well, I'll give you a hint.
-Okay.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.167
-I was in
"The Devil Wears Prada."

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.367
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.567
-Anne Hathaway?

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.667
-Close.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:24.901
Can Hathaway.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:31.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.801
-Can Hathaway.
-Hey, that actually reminds me,

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.033
I actually cooked something up
after the new year.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.334
And I think it's pretty crafty.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:38.467
-I can't wait to see.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.167
-Oh, well,
you're about to see it.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.934
I'm gonna see it as well.
These are my fun glasses.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.634
-Hello.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.067
Fashion police.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.267
No crime here.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.767
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, well...

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:52.868
-They're pretty easy to make.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.267
I just bedazzled
a leftover pair of glasses

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:56.868
from New Year's Eve, 2008.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.767
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.534
-I just love
that they're vintage.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.467
Hold on.
Let me take a mental picture.

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.400
Let me take another one.
-Yeah.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:11.968
Where are these going?

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:14.400
-I am posting those
on my brain Pinterest.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.534
-You can actually have
your own pair,

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:19.767
'cause I made two of these.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.767
-Oh, mylanta

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.701
-Try those on.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.167
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:30.200
-[ Singing ] I can see clearly
now that my glasses are on

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.300
-Stop it.
You're too much.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.767
I don't want my neighbor
complaining.

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:38.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.534
Well, it looks like we're down
to our last craft.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:41.534
-Oh, what is it?

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:42.968
-Well, here's a hint.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:45.567
It's cute.
It's got fruit.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.434
And it's perfect
for your tiny commute.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.901
-I give up.
-Look at that.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.601
-Look at that.
-Look at that.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.133
-I don't know what --

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.334
I didn't know how I was gonna
make that.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.734
Ta-da!

00:03:55.734 --> 00:04:00.367
Now don't be fooled because this
thing goes "berry" fast.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.968
I actually -- I actually drank a
5-hour energy

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:06.000
right before the show.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.234
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:08.501
-Well, I could just tell you
were on something.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:09.667
-You could, yeah.
-I could.

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:10.701
I could tell you were
on something.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:11.934
-If it lasts longer
than five hours,

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:14.234
I have to call a doctor.

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.701
-Well, I'll tell you what, that
little car just took a DNA test.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.567
-Uh-huh.
-And it came back that it is

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:21.200
100% that kitsch.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.868
-You want it?

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:28.534
-Are you saying what
I think you're saying?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.901
-Together: Craft swap!

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:33.167
-Here you go.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.000
-You want that--

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.734
Oh!

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:38.234
Actually --
Actually I like it --

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.033
You think maybe Diablo
can ride this?

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.267
-No, stop it.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.501
-Look at that.

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:45.601
That's what -- that's what
teamwork is right there.

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.167
There he goes.
Look at him there.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.234
-Wait a minute.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.734
-Diablo's not wearing
a seatbelt.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.734
Someone call Nine-Fun-Fun.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.601
-Well, it's Diablo's world,
we're just living in it.

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.567
That's all the time we have for
today's podcast.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.033
My thanks to Carole St. James.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.901
Carole, would you like
to join me --

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.767
Would you like to join me in
singing out to break?

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.467
-Does a raisin get an --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.868
Does a raisin get an invite
to a wrinkle convention?

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:14.734
-Here we go.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:18.000
One, two, three, four.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.067
[ Together ]
♪ Making little treasures ♪

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.601
♪ Out of little bits of trash ♪

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.734
♪ It's Todd Taft's
Odd Crafts... Podcast ♪

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:26.200
-Thank you so much, Carole.
It's a pleasure.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.567
I know you have Mod Podge all
over you, but this was great.

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:29.834
Look at Diablo.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:31.701
Diablo, he's a little rebel.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:32.701
He isn't wearing a seatbelt.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:33.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

